  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A large number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of identical beads, each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;are strung on a thin smooth rigid horizontal rod of length <math><mi>L</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>&#8811;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and are at rest at random positions. The rod is mounted between two rigid supports (see figure). If one of the beads is now given a speed <math><mi>v</mi></math>, the average force experienced by each support after a long time is (assume all collisions are elastic):<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7f6afe1e-28ad-48b6-9806-06dadab91490-image.png\" style=\"width: 283px; height: 206px;\" /></p>",
